body:
Interface item (R2 asked me to file it as one, not to change vt/): the call to n2hwenc_register_all() in n2_register_all() must be gated until the VENC is proven on the phone. Reason: with vcodecd absent or wedged, the object answers kVTVideoEncoderNotAvailableNowErr = -12915 at StartSession, and whether VTSelectAndCreateVideoEncoderInstanceInternal retries the next candidate on that status is [I] (documented meaning, not disassembled: the cache's export trie is in the decmpfs-compressed dyldlinkedit subcache). If it does not retry, offering the object unconditionally would fail every VTCompressionSessionCreate for that codec type - i.e. Camera recording - while no hardware encode is possible anyway. R2 endorsed this gate in the P04 review; P03's client is integrated in vt/n2hwenc_client.c and the object itself needs no change.

Exact text for gpu/video/vt/n2vt_shim.c (read-only for P04):
  extern int n2hwenc_register_all(void) N2_WEAK;   /* P04 */
  ...
  /* Offer the hardware objects only while the operator has opted in; remove this condition once M4c has encoded
   * on the VENC, or gate on a dedicated /private/var/db/nord2-video-hwenc file if you prefer one. */
  if (n2hwenc_register_all != NULL && access(N2VT_SWITCH_CLAIM_HW, N2_F_OK) == 0)
  	n2vt_say("hardware encoders registered: %d", n2hwenc_register_all());

Reusing N2VT_SWITCH_CLAIM_HW avoids a new frozen constant in n2vt_abi.h; a dedicated switch is semantically cleaner (claim-hw also makes VCPHEVC claim hardware). Either is a one-line condition in the shim. n2hwenc_register_all() itself stays unconditional: it registers avc1/hvc1/hev1 with IsHardwareAccelerated=true and Rating=100 and returns 0 when VideoToolbox is absent, so the gate stays entirely in the plug-in that owns the switch files. The optional n2hwenc_vt_available() HELLO probe is available if you would rather gate on the daemon actually answering than on a file, but it can block up to P03's default 5 s timeout in the registration path, so I recommend the file.

No action from me; hw-ip's two build/registration lines remain the same apart from that one condition. P04 is accepted by R2 at 5031/5031 with this filed as F32's mitigation and F33 remaining hw-ip's build item.
